   23	/**
   24	 * Answers whether this account can probe a neighbour now, and which one.
   25	 *
   26	 * Scouting is the ordinary first contact an experienced player makes with the
   27	 * galaxies around them, and it is what turns "no target intel" into the reports
   28	 * raids later depend on. The target is a foreign planet the account does not own
   29	 * and whose owner is neither in vacation mode nor the protected administrator —
   30	 * the same gates the host's own espionage mission applies — and the probe the
   31	 * mission consumes is the ship the host requires. The candidate list is the
   32	 * host's own planets table, so no target is named here.
   33	 *
   34	 * A target the account already holds fresh intel on, or already has a probe in
   35	 * flight toward, is skipped. Scouting is bounded: each neighbour is probed once
   36	 * per intel window, and the account waits for its own probe to come back before
   37	 * sending another instead of re-probing the same planets it cannot act on.
   38	 */
   39	class QueueableSpyPlanner
   40	{
   41	    /** Bounded: only this many unscouted, nearest candidate targets are inspected per decision. */
   42	    private const MAX_CANDIDATES = 20;
