  160	        // A scout looks at the quiet neighbours it has not already read, not at the closest rows in the
  161	        // universe: in a crowded universe the nearest bodies all belong to accounts that played minutes ago,
  162	        // so the activity star would refuse every one of them and the cap would never reach a farm. The
  163	        // candidate set is therefore a farm first and a neighbour second -- owners whose own last-activity
  164	        // stamp (the host's column) is oldest come first, and within that the nearest body to the origin wins
  165	        // (INT-003) -- and only then is the set capped. The stamp is the ordering key only; the host's
  166	        // isInactive() below stays the authority on whether a candidate really is a farm.
  167	        $home = $idleOrigins[0]->getPlanetCoordinates();
